<h1>TRadioButton</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveRadioButton" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveRadioButton</tt> is the active control counter part to <tt>TRadioButton</tt>.
The <tt>AutoPostBack</tt> property is set to true by default. Thus, when the radio button is clicked a
<tt>OnCallback</tt> event is raise after <tt>OnCheckedChanged</tt> event.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<table class="parameters">
<tr><th>Property</th><th>Effect on the browser</th></tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Checked</tt></td>
	<td>Selects or clears the button.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td><tt>Text</tt></td>
	<td>Replaces the content of the caption.</td>
</tr>
</table>

<p class="block-content">
Both updates are subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>GroupName</tt> cannot change during a callback. The grouping lives in the
<tt>name</tt> attribute of the input element, which a browser will not let script rewrite
once the element exists. Grouping is explained on
<a href="?page=Controls.RadioButton">TRadioButton</a>, including how the rendered name is
built and when <tt>UniqueGroupName</tt> is needed.
</p>

